  "elements": [
    {
      "id": "tPU6SPghjYXGgFw5flfHX",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 731.9997253417969,
      "y": -299.4997863769531,
      "width": 1140,
      "height": 1450,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 337986434,
      "version": 4149,
      "versionNonce": 1688945133,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793524435326,
      "created": 1793515330343,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Functional Requirement\n\n- User should able to create shortUrl out of any url.\n- User should be redirected from shortUrl to the original longUrl. \n- Url should be expirable after some point in time\n\nOut of scope \n- personalization\n\n\nNon- functional requirements\n- Scale Peak\n    - I wanted to start simple first \n        10K reads/sec , 1K writes/sec\n        Later scale it to 1M reads/sec, 10K writes/sec, Geo distribution\n-Latency \n    Read \n    - 20ms ->p95, 100ms ->p99\n    Write\n    - 200ms -> p95, 1s ->p99\n\n- HA system , Read your own write consistency, eventual visibility of new mappings to others reading from replica\n\n-Storage (assuming 1K new URLs/sec sustained; retention 1 week)\n    - 1,000 x 86,400 x 7 = 604.8M mappings retained\n    - 200 bytes x 604.8M = 120.96 GB raw (decimal units)\n    - Budget extra for metadata, indexes, replication and cleanup lag\n    - If 1K/sec is peak, size retained data using average creation rate\n\n- Acceptable Dataloss on primary failure\n\nOut of Scope \n- Telemetry \n- Analytics\n\n\nAPI \n\nCreate short URL (Idempotent using DB constraint)\n- POST /urls -> 201 Created\n  JSON body: { \"url\": \"https://example.com\", \"expiryAt\": \"<timestamp>\" }\n  Response includes the generated shortUrl\n\nGet Long url redirection\n-GET /{shortCode} -> Redirect 302 with cache control : no-store with long url \nor 404 for expired links\n\nTradeOffs\n301-> less server load, but load expired links\n302-> more server laad, but expiry links are handled appropiately.\n\nRYOW -> read from replica, if 404 fallback to primary , tradeoff -> 2 reads in 404\n\nFor expiry -> best effort TTL index + return 410 if expired in hot path.\n\nHigh Level Design Diagram (Starting Scale)\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Functional Requirement\n\n- User should able to create shortUrl out of any url.\n- User should be redirected from shortUrl to the original longUrl. \n- Url should be expirable after some point in time\n\nOut of scope \n- personalization\n\n\nNon- functional requirements\n- Scale Peak\n    - I wanted to start simple first \n        10K reads/sec , 1K writes/sec\n        Later scale it to 1M reads/sec, 10K writes/sec, Geo distribution\n-Latency \n    Read \n    - 20ms ->p95, 100ms ->p99\n    Write\n    - 200ms -> p95, 1s ->p99\n\n- HA system , Read your own write consistency, eventual visibility of new mappings to others reading from replica\n\n-Storage (assuming 1K new URLs/sec sustained; retention 1 week)\n    - 1,000 x 86,400 x 7 = 604.8M mappings retained\n    - 200 bytes x 604.8M = 120.96 GB raw (decimal units)\n    - Budget extra for metadata, indexes, replication and cleanup lag\n    - If 1K/sec is peak, size retained data using average creation rate\n\n- Acceptable Dataloss on primary failure\n\nOut of Scope \n- Telemetry \n- Analytics\n\n\nAPI \n\nCreate short URL (Idempotent using DB constraint)\n- POST /urls -> 201 Created\n  JSON body: { \"url\": \"https://example.com\", \"expiryAt\": \"<timestamp>\" }\n  Response includes the generated shortUrl\n\nGet Long url redirection\n-GET /{shortCode} -> Redirect 302 with cache control : no-store with long url \nor 404 for expired links\n\nTradeOffs\n301-> less server load, but load expired links\n302-> more server laad, but expiry links are handled appropiately.\n\nRYOW -> read from replica, if 404 fallback to primary , tradeoff -> 2 reads in 404\n\nFor expiry -> best effort TTL index + return 410 if expired in hot path.\n\nHigh Level Design Diagram (Starting Scale)\n\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
