    {
      "id": "jhvjQsoBQYin2P8vGqTF_",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1624,
      "y": 1521.0001831054688,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 125,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aK",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1846044546,
      "version": 164,
      "versionNonce": 968370211,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793524266689,
      "created": 1793520441791,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Run each minute to clean up expired records.\n- Check expiryAt on every redirect lookup, before redirecting.\n- The daemon reclaims storage; it does not enforce exact expiry.\n- Avoid full scans: assess expiryAt indexing or native TTL.\n- With multiple sidecars, coordinate work or make deletion idempotent.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Run each minute to clean up expired records.\n- Check expiryAt on every redirect lookup, before redirecting.\n- The daemon reclaims storage; it does not enforce exact expiry.\n- Avoid full scans: assess expiryAt indexing or native TTL.\n- With multiple sidecars, coordinate work or make deletion idempotent.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "review_latency_scope",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2480,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 920,
      "height": 200,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aL",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 312151083,
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 2077953187,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793520576336,
      "created": 1793520537590,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "REVIEW - LATENCY AND CAPACITY\n\nYour p95 / p99 targets are recorded in the requirements.\nStill define where the timer starts and stops:\nserver processing, or client-to-service round trip?\nRedirect latency should exclude loading the destination page.\nClarify whether request rates are average or peak.\nValidate capacity under load; storage size alone is not sufficient.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "REVIEW - LATENCY AND CAPACITY\n\nYour p95 / p99 targets are recorded in the requirements.\nStill define where the timer starts and stops:\nserver processing, or client-to-service round trip?\nRedirect latency should exclude loading the destination page.\nClarify whether request rates are average or peak.\nValidate capacity under load; storage size alone is not sufficient.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "review_consistency",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2480,
      "y": 270,
      "width": 920,
      "height": 200,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aM",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 569781864,
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 212058893,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793520576336,
      "created": 1793520537590,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "REVIEW - CONSISTENCY\n\nRead-your-writes protects the creator's subsequent reads.\nA recipient may still miss a newly created mapping on a lagging replica.\nDecide whether immediately shared links must work for everyone.\nSpecify how creator reads reach data that includes their write.\nThe insert-if-absent operation must be authoritative for the code;\neventually consistent reads alone cannot prevent duplicate allocation.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "REVIEW - CONSISTENCY\n\nRead-your-writes protects the creator's subsequent reads.\nA recipient may still miss a newly created mapping on a lagging replica.\nDecide whether immediately shared links must work for everyone.\nSpecify how creator reads reach data that includes their write.\nThe insert-if-absent operation must be authoritative for the code;\neventually consistent reads alone cannot prevent duplicate allocation.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "review_availability",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2480,
      "y": 540,
      "width": 920,
      "height": 175,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aN",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 244990118,
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 1387757635,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793520576336,
      "created": 1793520537590,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "REVIEW - AVAILABILITY\n\nThe load balancer, 3 stateless instances and replicas are now shown.\nStill define health checks, failover and failure-domain placement.\nClarify primary / replica roles and sync versus async replication.\nDecide acceptable data loss and recovery time on primary failure.\nEnsure load balancing itself remains available on instance failure.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "REVIEW - AVAILABILITY\n\nThe load balancer, 3 stateless instances and replicas are now shown.\nStill define health checks, failover and failure-domain placement.\nClarify primary / replica roles and sync versus async replication.\nDecide acceptable data loss and recovery time on primary failure.\nEnsure load balancing itself remains available on instance failure.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "review_expiration",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2480,
      "y": 790,
      "width": 920,
      "height": 175,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aO",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1741686258,
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 1991367021,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793520576336,
      "created": 1793520537590,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "REVIEW - EXPIRATION\n\nServe a redirect only when now < expiryAt.\nAn expired record can remain stored until background cleanup runs.\nChoose the response for expired / missing codes (for example 410 / 404).\nDecide whether expired short codes can ever be reused;\nreuse could send an old shared link to a different destination.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "REVIEW - EXPIRATION\n\nServe a redirect only when now < expiryAt.\nAn expired record can remain stored until background cleanup runs.\nChoose the response for expired / missing codes (for example 410 / 404).\nDecide whether expired short codes can ever be reused;\nreuse could send an old shared link to a different destination.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    }
  ],
